<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heiligenkreuz Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1133</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heiligenkreuz Abbey is a Cistercian monastery in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> Woods, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a>, founded in 1133 by Margrave Leopold III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. It is the oldest continuously inhabited Cistercian monastery in the world and holds the tombs of several Babenberg rulers. Its church combines Romanesque and Gothic parts, and it runs a pontifical university.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heiligenkreuz-abbey.jpg" alt="Heiligenkreuz Abbey" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C.Stadler/Bwag · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heiligenkreuz_-_Stift,_Luftaufnahme.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
